BUILD_ONLY: the TopoGym image is never pushed to a registry (docs/rcb/PROTOCOL.md §2.4, D5). Every evaluation host builds
it locally under the name the task packages use; Harbor finds it in the local Docker image store.

Why
  The image contains the Nyx renderer (TopoGym's RGB observations and replay videos), whose redistribution terms are not
  confirmed yet (scripts/push_images.sh refuses to push it). The rest is Genesis 1.2.1 (Apache-2.0), libuipc built from
  source with the determinism patches in uipc-patches/, PyTorch (BSD) and the pip packages in requirements/*.lock.

Which image
  The name is whatever the task packages FROM; in a helper release tree all packages name one image:
    IMG=$(grep -h '^FROM' tasks/*-privileged/environment/Dockerfile | sort -u | awk '{print $2}'); echo "$IMG"
  It must be built from the same tree as the packages (the release's source commit): a package records the simulator
  source hash, dependency versions and libuipc recipe it was frozen against (environment/runtime_binding.json) and every
  session refuses to start in an image that differs. The image Id is not part of that check, so a local build is fine.

Host
  Linux x86_64 (not WSL: Nyx needs the NVIDIA Vulkan driver inside the container), an NVIDIA GPU with driver >= 580,
  Docker with BuildKit and the NVIDIA Container Toolkit. BuildKit must use the default `docker` driver
  (`docker buildx ls`: the current builder's driver is `docker`), otherwise the task images cannot FROM a local image.
  Build: about 60 GB of free disk (the image is 11.2 GB, plus the libuipc builder stage and BuildKit's cache). libuipc's
  CUDA compile dominates: UIPC_BUILD_JOBS (default 3) sets its parallelism, more needs more RAM; our 2026-10-05 build with
  16 jobs and a warm vcpkg cache took 15 minutes, a cold build takes longer (not measured). Network access to docker.io,
  pypi.org, download.pytorch.org, github.com (libuipc and vcpkg sources) and dl.polyhaven.org (the CC0 studio HDRI).
  No account, key or token is needed.
  Running needs no network for the simulator.

Build (from the repository root)
  docker build --build-arg UIPC_BUILD_JOBS=8 -f images/topogym/Dockerfile -t "$IMG" .

Check a build (the line it prints goes into MANIFEST.md, "images:")
  docker run --rm "$IMG" python -c 'import json; from topogym.simulator.frozen_binding import installed_runtime; print(json.dumps(installed_runtime(), sort_keys=True))' > image_runtime.json
  python3 -c 'import glob, json, sys; want = json.load(open(sorted(glob.glob("tasks/*/environment/runtime_binding.json"))[0]))["runtime"]; sys.exit(0 if json.load(open("image_runtime.json")) == want else "image differs from the tasks runtime binding: do not run")' \
    && echo "$IMG $(docker image inspect --format '{{.Id}}' "$IMG") runtime matches the tasks"
